To find the average highest temperature, we need to add up all the temperatures and then divide by the number of countries. We can do this as follows:
\begin{align*}
-48 + 21 + (-3) &= -20 \\
\text{The sum of the temperatures is } -20 \text{ degrees Fahrenheit}.
\end{align*}
Now, we'll divide the sum by the number of countries (which is 3):
\begin{align*}
\frac{-20}{3} &\approx -6.67
\end{align*}
Therefore, the average highest temperature of these three countries is approximately -6.67 degrees Fahrenheit.
